DSH-Android patch 28: llm-service-lite (vendored @snnh/dsh-llm-service-lite 0.2.1), the output-cap field a
chat-completions endpoint takes. Applies on top of 14 to 27.

The adapter always asks for `max_tokens`. OpenAI's reasoning models, and gateways that forward to them
(a relay in front of OpenAI, Azure, Bedrock), refuse it with 400 "Unsupported parameter: 'max_tokens' is
not supported with this model. Use 'max_completion_tokens' instead", so every chat to such a model failed.
Which field an endpoint takes cannot be told from its address (a relay hides what is behind it), so the
adapter learns it from the refusal: a 400 whose text names the field is asked once more with the other
spelling, and the endpoint remembers it for the rest of the process. The reverse refusal ("unknown field
max_completion_tokens") flips it back. Requests that never meet the refusal are unchanged.
